      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I encountered this recently; specifically, if you are banned from a group, you can click the block button for that group, and it will add that group to your block list.\n\nHowever, you will not receive visual confirmation that you have successfully blocked the group, and the Block button will remain in the top right corner.\n\nAttempting to block the group again will result in a silent 403 error with the message \"You must leave a group before blocking it․\".\n\nAttempting to unblock the group to remove them from your blocked groups will also fail with a different silent 403 error \"You don't have permission to do that․\"\n\nBesides the poor UX and lack of direct user-facing error messages, the main negative effects of this bug are that the group is permanently stuck in your block list, and you are forced to see them in there forever, and the fact that it leaks the information that you are indeed banned from that group. As I understand it, you are not actually supposed to be able to tell if you've been banned from a group or not.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
